Id: lin033w
Severity: WARN
Category: network
Check: check_sysctl
Fix: Set net.ipv4.icmp_ignore_bogus_error_responses=1 in /etc/sysctl.d.
References: sysctl.d(5); Linux kernel ip-sysctl documentation
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST CM-6, SC-7; ISO 8.20; CE Secure configuration

net.ipv4.icmp_ignore_bogus_error_responses is 0, so malformed ICMP error
responses from broken routers are logged, which lets anyone fill the
log:
  # sysctl -w net.ipv4.icmp_ignore_bogus_error_responses=1
